             572                     
             573                           t2v = sfctmp * (1.0 + 0.61*q2)
             574                     
             575                     !  --- ...  next call routine sfcdif to calculate the sfc exchange coef (ch)
             576                     !           for heat and moisture.
             577                     !    note - comment out call sfcdif, if sfcdif already called in calling
             578                     !           program (such as in coupled atmospheric model).
             579                     !         - do not call sfcdif until after above call to redprm, in case
             580                     !           alternative values of roughness length (z0) and zilintinkevich
             581                     !           coef (czil) are set there via namelist i/o.
             582                     !         - routine sfcdif returns a ch that represents the wind spd times
             583                     !           the "original" nondimensional "ch" typical in literature.  hence
             584                     !           the ch returned from sfcdif has units of m/s.  the important
             585                     !           companion coefficient of ch, carried here as "rch", is the ch
             586                     !           from sfcdif times air density and parameter "cp".  "rch" is
             587                     !           computed in "call penman". rch rather than ch is the coeff
             588                     !           usually invoked later in eqns.
             589                     !         - sfcdif also returns the surface exchange coefficient for momentum,
             590                     !           cm, also known as the surface drage coefficient, but cm is not
